WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:05.990
So this is pretty wild in another one of these
sort of Dr. Jekyll and Mr. Hyde moments on

00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:09.450
Fox News, Trump daughter in law and campaign
employee.

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:10.970
I think she's an advisor.

00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:13.030
Lara Lara Trump.

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:16.010
This is the wife of Eric Trump, not known
as the smart one.

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:22.050
Eric, that is, she ran up against what I guess
now counts as news on Fox News.

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:27.060
And she was instantly reality checked by Fox
News host Martha MacCallum about her continued

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:30.080
claims that it's actually Donald Trump who
won the election.

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:32.220
We all know that Joe Biden won.

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:36.149
There's not anything that Laura or Donald
Trump or Eric Trump are going to be able to

00:00:36.149 --> 00:00:37.149
do about it.

00:00:37.149 --> 00:00:42.310
Now, the discussion was actually about the
upcoming runoff Senate elections in Georgia.

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:47.309
And recently the question was posed to the
RNC chairwoman, Ronna McDaniel.

00:00:47.309 --> 00:00:53.550
Can you trust the Georgia election, given
all of the fraud you claim took place at the

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:56.100
presidential election level in Georgia?

00:00:56.100 --> 00:01:00.629
And Martha MacCallum rightly brings up, you
know, there could be Republican voters who

00:01:00.629 --> 00:01:05.950
are hearing from Trump and others about how
we can't trust the election results in Georgia.

00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:10.590
They may just stay home if they believe their
vote won't be fairly counted.

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:16.530
And Laura Trump actually takes issue, not
with Ranna saying maybe that's true, but with

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:19.950
Martha MacCallum, presuming that Donald Trump
lost the election.

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:24.229
And when she tries to pull this out, Martha
MacCallum brutally confronts Laura Trump with

00:01:24.229 --> 00:01:27.610
the reality that states have certified Joe
Biden's wins.

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:28.970
There's nothing else to do.

00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:31.389
You can't squeeze any more water out of that
rock.

00:01:31.389 --> 00:01:32.389
Take a look at how it goes.

00:01:32.389 --> 00:01:34.249
They're saying, why should we even go out?

00:01:34.249 --> 00:01:35.279
This has already decided.

00:01:35.279 --> 00:01:36.530
Why should we bother?

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:43.219
So that sounds to me like a pretty good cocktail
for having a lot of Republican voters who

00:01:43.219 --> 00:01:46.869
support the president stay home and then he's
not going to get what he wants, which is to

00:01:46.869 --> 00:01:49.829
have his legacy protected by these senators.

00:01:49.829 --> 00:01:54.159
Well, look, I still think that the president
will get four more years in office.

00:01:54.159 --> 00:01:57.170
I think it'll be the next four years because
this thing is far from over.

00:01:57.170 --> 00:01:58.170
All right.

00:01:58.170 --> 00:01:59.170
Just had certification.

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:04.049
Today in Arizona and Georgia, in Wisconsin,
you heard Moraldo moments ago say, you know,

00:02:04.049 --> 00:02:06.359
it's time to accept the outcome of this.

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:10.590
What what are you seeing or hearing out there
that that he is not?

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:13.250
Well, those certifications are just procedural
steps.

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:19.459
And the reality is the Electoral College does
not vote in their states until December 14th.

00:02:19.459 --> 00:02:22.879
Congress doesn't actually certify anything
until the beginning of January.

00:02:22.879 --> 00:02:25.129
So we've got plenty of time.

00:02:25.129 --> 00:02:29.379
Sadly, we have become accustomed to having
to work twice as hard, three times as hard

00:02:29.379 --> 00:02:31.849
as a normal candidate or normal campaign.

00:02:31.849 --> 00:02:35.209
But we're we're prepared for this and we're
prepared for the fight.

00:02:35.209 --> 00:02:40.939
So understand that our standards are so low
for what we would expect on FOX News that

00:02:40.939 --> 00:02:42.659
this sort of counts as pushback.

00:02:42.659 --> 00:02:47.230
I mean, it's laughable, but it's good that
some people on Fox are doing this.

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:52.160
But the bar is so low for what counts as holding
people accountable.

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:56.550
The casual nature with which these people
continue to claim that essentially down is

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:58.590
up, black is white.

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:01.100
Trump won and Biden lost again.

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:03.690
It's been normalized to some degree.

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:09.569
In some circles, it is now normal to say Trump
won an election that he actually lost.

00:03:09.569 --> 00:03:15.210
Now, there is something to glean from what
Laura Trump says when she says the Electoral

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:18.360
College doesn't certify until December 14th.

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:20.920
What she's saying is we are going to draw
this out.

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:23.350
This nonsense will be drawn out as long as
possible.

00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:25.780
Now, will it end on December 14th?

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:26.780
It's unclear.

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:30.079
This phase might end, but they might come
up with something else to keep going with,

00:03:30.079 --> 00:03:34.830
maybe until the Georgia Senate election on
January 5th, maybe even until Joe Biden's

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:37.609
inauguration on January 20th, maybe even beyond.

00:03:37.609 --> 00:03:38.739
Who the hell knows?

00:03:38.739 --> 00:03:41.609
But back to Fox News just for a moment.

00:03:41.609 --> 00:03:45.950
We now live in a world where, compared to
tens of millions of people, Fox News is the

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:47.269
voice of reason.

00:03:47.269 --> 00:03:52.239
What I mean is we believe, based on the latest
polls, that 80 percent of Trump voters believe

00:03:52.239 --> 00:03:53.900
Trump won.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.879
They believe something that's just not true.

00:03:55.879 --> 00:03:57.239
That's about 75 million.

00:03:57.239 --> 00:03:58.840
I'm sorry, that's about 60 million people.

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:03.849
80 percent of Trump's 75 million voters believe
Trump won FOX News.

00:04:03.849 --> 00:04:07.999
Daytime is the voice of reason on that issue.

00:04:07.999 --> 00:04:11.719
Relative to 60 million people.

00:04:11.719 --> 00:04:18.440
Fox News daytime is more tethered to reality
than 60 million people on this issue.

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:19.769
That is stunning.

